.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt UPDATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm update
.Nd periodically synchronize cached writes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
takes no arguments.
Init starts one instance at boot on every image and keeps it running.
It repeatedly sleeps for thirty seconds and calls
.Xr sync 2
to write cached data to disk, whether or not another program calls
.Xr sync 2 .
.Pp
The kernel does not perform this periodic sync itself: its timer
cannot sleep, and it has no thread of its own for this work.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sync 2 ,
.Xr init 8
